olution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$22$** | **$25$** | **$28$** | **$34$** | **$40$** |\n| $y$ | $12$ | $14$ | $16$ | $19$ | $24$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 25 \\\\ 3 & 28 \\\\ 4 & 34 \\\\ 5 & 40\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 19 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eaee4e9-7be5-5c35-bc88-89697a15d75a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression That Passes Through the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d634898-d03f-52e0-a7f5-4c9a5ea81f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 15 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 18 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 22 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400861} {:answer/id #uuid "8664c14d-06e4-5328-b2d6-7aa2947357a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400862} {:answer/id #uuid "67c2c7b9-1f3c-57c7-aba2-af5fc8364720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 15 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 18 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 22 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400863} {:answer/id #uuid "6e19eb4b-b77c-58a6-9771-ee8238bdab0d" :answe