 **$22$** |\n| ${x}_{3}$ | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$3$** | **$7$** | **$12$** |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n\n \nThe coefficients of the hyperplane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}_{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 15 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 18 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 22 & 12\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eaee4e9-7be5-5c35-bc88-89697a15d75a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression That Passes Through the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e8854f2-d953-5755-bbd4-ba8c165a0a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 30 & 45 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 20 & 54 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 65 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 77 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 90 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400868} {:answer/id #uuid "0f7fdf21-b096-5d7c-9388-7dd869ebc9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 30 & 45 \\\\ 2 & 20 & 54 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 65 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 77 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 90\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400869} {:answer/id #uuid "2287d534-3da3-5304-985f-1fa9431bb2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400870} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c200c8-701d-5c4e-935d-58a54ed49199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[